⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of WSL2 is a VM; Docker isn't
node CG1 · CG1 · ⟦WSL2 is a VM; Docker isn't:CG1:03c757⟧

WHO   — WSL2 is a VM; Docker isn't — The accuracy point: WSL2 is a REAL lightweight Hyper-V VM with its own Linux kernel (a true nesting level); a Docker container is OS-isolation (namespaces+cgroups) that SHARES the host kernel. So Docker Desktop on Windows adds a VM (it runs inside WSL2); plain Docker on Linux adds zero.
